# Pre-mortem — V2i onboarding dance
- date: 2026-09-27
- branch: fix/cli-254-v2i-onboarding-dance
- lenses: [gary-klein, saltzer-schroeder, tony-hoare]

## Risks

### R1 — Klein (change impact)
Change scope: one lib function extension (drive_start) + one env
export in entry.sh V2i wrapper. Fake_claude tests default to 0 = no
dance. Adopter machines untouched. Impact: real-claude V2i drives only.

### R2 — Klein (unmet prerequisite)
Dance assumes 2 Enters clears onboarding. If Claude renders 3+ screens,
drives still time out. Falsification: drive.log after CI run.
Cure path: bump SMOKE_DRIVE_ONBOARDING_ENTERS to 3, or send a
non-Enter keystroke, per drive.log content.

### R3 — Klein (spurious READY still matches)
The default READY pattern (READY>|>) may still match on `>` characters
in the post-Enter screens (e.g., syntax preview or REPL cursor). If
drive_send fires before Claude is at REPL, drives still fail.
Falsification: drive.log will show drive_send output landing in the
wrong screen state.
Cure: tighten catalog READY patterns to REPL-specific glyphs in a
follow-on (e.g., match on the actual REPL frame chars).

### R4 — Hoare (postcondition on drive_start)
drive_start's postcondition is unchanged when the env var is 0 (queue
file starts with preamble + spawn only, same as before). When the env
var is >0, the postcondition extends with N sleeps + N sends. Tests
pin both cases.

### R5 — Saltzer-Schroeder (least privilege)
Dance sends only Enter keys. No shell injection surface — the raw
string `\r` is written literally to the queue file. Env var is
integer-checked; non-numeric input silently falls to 0 (bash test
`[ "$var" -gt 0 ] 2>/dev/null`).

### R6 — Klein (fake_claude test drift)
If a future test enables the dance (SMOKE_DRIVE_ONBOARDING_ENTERS>0)
against fake_claude, fake will echo RESP: lines for each dance Enter,
which will shift the DONE match into wrong lines. Mitigation: tests
default to 0. Documented in the dance comment.

## Strongest concerns folded in
- R2 (Enter count) — falsification path via drive.log.
- R3 (spurious READY) — flagged as follow-on cure if R2 clears but
  drives still fail on the DONE pattern.

## Verdict
Ship. Risks are bounded, observable via drive.log, and each has a
named cure path.
